gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":95.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.57849,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.2,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":20.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Karat Packaging Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the manufacture and distribution of single-use disposable products in plastic, paper, biopolymer-based, and other compostable forms used in various restaurant and foodservice settings. It offers food and take-out containers, bags, boxes, tableware, cups, lids, cutlery, straws, specialty beverage ingredients, gloves, utensils, janitorial and warehouse supplies, and other products under the Karat Earth brand. The company also distributes food and beverage items, such as syrups, boba tea, and coffee drinks; and provides new product development, design, printing, and logistics services. It offers its products to national and regional distributors, restaurant chains, retail establishments, and online customers. Karat Packaging Inc. was founded in 2000 and is based in Chino, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Alan  Yu | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 55 | Compensation: $337,500 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 636 people. Revenue per employee of $735K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $52K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Karat Packaging Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $669M market cap on $468M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $33M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 20\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 58% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 76% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7607217063304651},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.2},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Karat Packaging's (NASDAQ:KRT) Earnings Are Weaker Than They Seem","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-krt/karat-packaging/news/karat-packagings-nasdaqkrt-earnings-are-weaker-than-they-see","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794564601.603,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to KRT Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/Technical_Reactions_to_KRT_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111226070401_1794485041.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794485041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Karat Packaging (NASDAQ:KRT) Stock Price Up 10.1% \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/karat-packaging-nasdaqkrt-stock-price-up-10-1-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794243783.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"KRT Q3 2026 deep dive: margin pressures persist as new accounts and supply chain actions take center stage","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/krt-q3-2026-deep-dive-120536820.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794225936.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Did Karat Packaging (KRT) Stock Drop Today?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/s